      "message": "fix(tofu): read AKS OIDC issuer from infra-bootstrap remote state\n\nFollow-up to #37, which switched the federated identity credential's\n`issuer` to `data.azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.infra.oidc_issuer_url`.\nThat data source 404s because the cluster lives in subscription\n606a1ca1 (romaine-life) while this stack authenticates against\naee0cbd2 (Azure subscription 1). Same failure mode diagrams/tofu hits.\n\nSwitch to reading `aks_oidc_issuer_url` from infra-bootstrap's tfstate\noutput instead. The tfstate blob is in this subscription's storage\naccount (nelsontofu) and the CI principal already has access to it\n(that's where this stack's own state lives). Matches glimmung's\npattern in glimmung/tofu/remote-state.tf, which has been working.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
